From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Audit Hub <audit-hub@audit-hub.invalid>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 17:50:03 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 09/10] feat(account): let people delete their account, and
 admins delete others

The schema already cascaded a user's rows, but nothing deleted an
account, so the right to erasure had no way in, and an admin could not
remove someone who left.

POST /api/account/deletion deletes the signed-in person's account with
the current password (limited like a sign-in), clears the browser's
cookies and signs every tab out; the sign-in page then says so.
DELETE /api/users/:id (admins only, not their own account) deletes
another one. Either runs in one transaction under the admins' locks
(the last admin who may sign in cannot be deleted, nor two admins
delete each other at once) and the account's: its sessions, links and
queued messages go with it, invitations it sent keep no sender, its
access tokens stop at once. A new account_deleted notice (an enum value:
an expand step) goes to the former address, queued without the user
the deletion would take it along with, and carries no link.

The lock helpers of the admin who always remains move to users/admins.ts.
The account page's password-change specs scope their fields to their
form, as the deletion form asks for the current password too.

