+### Account deletion
+
+A person deletes their own account from the Account page (`POST /api/account/deletion`, with the
+current password, limited like a sign-in, after a confirmation); an admin deletes another one from
+its page (`DELETE /api/users/:id`). In one transaction, under the admins' locks for an admin and
+the account's lock, the row goes and the schema cascades the rest: sessions, one-time links and
+queued messages go with it, and invitations it sent keep no sender. The last admin who may sign
+in cannot be deleted, so two admins deleting each other at once cannot both succeed. A notice is
+queued to the former address (`account_deleted`, queued without the user, as the deletion would
+take it along); it carries no link, and tells the owner what to do if they did not delete it. The
+account's access tokens stop at once (the guard finds no account), the browser's cookies are
+cleared, and every tab is signed out. What the application keeps elsewhere about the person
+(logs, backups, other systems) is the project's to erase: see the privacy notice it publishes.
+
